course: dictionary
lesson: 13427
title: Words for people who love home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A homebody is a person who likes staying at home more than going out. The word is informal, and people use it mainly in the US. «Mia is a homebody, so she would rather watch a film on the sofa than go to the party.» The clue is the rest of the sentence: she chooses the sofa over the party, so homebody must mean someone who likes home.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. Swap in your idea of the word and read the sentence again. «Dad is a homebody and loves his armchair by the fire.» If homebody means someone who likes staying in, the sentence makes sense.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole and Badger are homebodies who love their snug houses. Toad always rushes about, so he is not a homebody. The story shows you the difference through what each character does.
fact: A homebody is a person who likes staying at home more than going out.
fact: Homebody is informal, and it is used mainly in the US.
fact: In the UK, people may say «home-lover» or «stay-at-home» instead.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole and Badger are homebodies, and Toad always rushes about.
exercise: «Mia is a homebody, so she would rather watch a film on the sofa than go to the party.» What is a homebody? | A person who sells furniture | A person who builds houses | A person who is always travelling | *A person who likes staying at home more than going out
exercise: Which UK phrase means the same as homebody? | *Stay-at-home | Sea captain | Globe-trotter | Night owl
exercise: In The Wind in the Willows, which character always rushes about instead of staying home? | Badger | *Toad | Mole
test: Which person is most likely to be a homebody? | Someone who goes to the park every morning | Someone who sails round the world | Someone who climbs mountains each summer | *Someone who loves cosy evenings reading by the fire
test: A homebody is the opposite of which kind of person? | A person who loves a warm bed | A person who loves quiet evenings in | A person who loves a cosy sofa | *A person who loves going out and exploring
exam: Which sentence uses homebody correctly? | *Dad is a homebody, so he would rather stay in and read than go out. | Dad is a homebody, so he runs a marathon every Sunday. | Dad is a homebody, so he sails across the sea each week. | Dad is a homebody, so he is always at the airport.
